{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1041983-and-then-there-was-darkness-mythology-thread-just-for-fun","id":1041983,"title":"And Then, There Was Darkness [mythology thread, Just For Fun!]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-01T13:05:37-08:00","id":1041983,"title":"And Then, There Was Darkness [mythology thread, Just For Fun!]","content":"<b><u>Time of Creation</u></b><br /> <br /> <i>And then, there was Darkness. And the Darkness slithered and coiled, twisted and danced, flowing upon the ruins of what was before. It was free, without form, without limit. Everything was the Darkness, and the Darkness feasted upon itself. However, there was only so much one could gain from self loath- the Darkness desired for a far richer menu. It desired chaos, pain, suffering, fear. It wanted despair, lust, sin and isolation. It was all- yet by its own, without anything to stand against, it was nothing.<br /> <br /> Motivated by those desires, the Darkness made a gambit- it had to sacrifice a portion of its own power, giving existence to things which were not Darkness, and in exchange it would be able to torment the new life which would be birthed from it. However, by doing so, it had to give power to those who would consider it enemies, making it vulnerable to those which were not Darkness. Yet the temptation was too great for it to ignore, as even the Darkness was not willing to spend eternity in silent solitude with no pain or suffering. <br /> <br /> Swirling around itself, the Darkness started to fold its silken cloaks, gathering the nothingness which is all and giving birth to thing which are from the ruins of what was once before. And from the ruins, things took shape and form, materializing from the primordial void. Everywhere the Darkness moved itself, things were formed- earth rose as solid, winds started to blow, water started to storm. The power of creation was great and painful, and the Darkness suffered a pain of thousand years as it gave birth for what that is from what that wasn't- and as it did, it swore its creation would suffer thousand times more. Finally, when its creation was formed, the Darkness embraced it as a newborn baby, enveloping it with its dark tendrils.<br /> <br /> Feeling the touch of another, the earth and sky and sea looked upon its maker and asked &quot;who am I?&quot;<br /> <br /> Tired from the birth of thousand years, the Darkness painfully replied &quot;you are the World&quot;.<br /> <br /> Yet, the Darkness was yet to finish- for the World was cold and hostile, empty and null. It required to define itself, and so the Darkness twisted once more, gathering its shrouds from above the world and created a void which was not Darkness- a light which was not light, for the sun was yet to shine in that primordial world. And where the light which was not light touched the World, things started to stir- ideas were birthed, principles were established, things were define beyond any possible doubt. The light which was not light burned the Darkness, for its was not to be defined or understood, and the Darkness cursed its painful touch and hide itself beyond the World- taking refuge behind its rocks and mountains as long lines of darkness which was not Darkness any longer.<br /> <br /> Requiring definition light which was not light shined as it asked &quot;who am I?&quot;<br /> <br /> Staring hatefully from beyond the mountains, the Darkness resentfully replied &quot;you are the Truth&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200bMimicking the sibling who gave it life, the darkness which was not darkness asked &quot;who am I?&quot;<br /> <br /> Whispering to it carefully, the Darkness silently replied &quot;you are the Shadow&quot;<br /> <br /> And the Darkness called the time of the Truth and Shadow as day, and divided the time of Truth from the time of Darkness- half of all time which was, is and will be was given to the siblings, dooming them to an ever lasting battle which would never be decided. And the other half of all time, the Darkness took for itself, and named it as night. Wishing to banish the light which was not light yet burned it so much, the Darkness spread itself once more, covering the sky and earth and sea of the World as it desired to start its reign of tyranny. Yet, as it called upon the night, strange light pierced through the Darkness, cutting it like broken glass. Stars shined like gemstones in the primordial darkness- a light which was light, and which held the ideas and principles of the Truth as what it planned each night before the time of day.<br /> <br /> Watching coldly upon the earth, the stars asked with maddening voices &quot;who am I?&quot;<br /> <br /> Angry from the unexpected twist of events, and Darkness confusingly replied &quot;you are Fate&quot;<br /> <br /> And the night and day has passed, moving as the Darkness roamed through the World in search for an haven from the burning light of the Truth- yet everywhere it moved, the World ripped through its tender mists with burning earth and frozen blizzards, storming seas and empty light. &quot;Why do you do this?&quot; the Darkness asked the world &quot;I am your mother and father, giving you existence and meaning. Why do you hurt me so much?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I do not&quot; the World replied &quot;for it is not me- but your own pain of birth, which you cursed me with once I was born&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;In that case, I shall take away your pain&quot; the Darkness ruthlessly replied &quot;and I'll name it Terror&quot;, and with that, Terror came and screamed with pleasure, </i><i>trembling the World and feasting upon its pain. Seeing how it tormented her child, the Darkness looked with envy and said &quot;The World is mine, for I am its mother and father. Its pain is my own to feast upon, and blood is mine to drink. I shall not give you free hand with the World, Terror, for you are my child too&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;You call me child, yet I am not yours&quot; Terror arrogantly replied &quot;I am free to do as I please, for I am the pain of the World itself. Every wound of the World is my own flesh, every blow is my own blood. I feast upon the World's suffering, and I'll upon yours, too!&quot;<br /> <br /> And the Terror called, trembling the earth and sky and sea and causing them to scream with pain- but the Darkness didn't wavered, for the Darkness knew the Terror for what it was. &quot;You are every wound ever given to the World&quot; it replied &quot;your hunger knows no limits, you desire for pain is brutal and hollow. Yet wounds can heal, too- and I shall give you that gift, my child, for pain without cure eventually fades to the Darkness&quot;<br /> <br /> And the Darkness called upon the night, and Fate shined in the heavens. &quot;What you wish for, mother and father?&quot; Fate asked, and the Darkness replied &quot;to give meaning for the suffering of the world, child&quot;. Sending its formless arms, the Darkness moved the starts out of alignment, writing new fate for those which are yet to be born. And as it did, things has started to flow upon the World- rivers of movement and change. Every time the Terror hit the World, the rivers shifted their course, and with each wound it caused, they learned. Slowly, they healed the wounds and covered the scars, growing trees and mosses and fungi around the Terror, trapping it with vines and leaves and branches. The Terror screamed with frustration- yet for no use. Every wound it caused only made the rivers learn better, every pain it inflicted only made them stronger.<br /> <br /> Softly, the many growing rivers asked with slow, comforting voice &quot;who am I?&quot;<br /> <br /> Pleasured with the outcome, the Darkness sweetly replied &quot;you are Life&quot;<br /> <br /> While happy with its child, the Darkness knew that left out of control, Life would grow beyond its goal of maintaining Terror in check and healing the World's wounds, but may even triumph over the Darkness itself. To avoid that future, the Darkness dived to the depth of the World's sea, seeking for the darkness from beyond the world which was hidden in there from before all creation. It took the cold waters of the abyss, and during the darkest night it crawled back to the surface and poured them upon the World' earth.<br /> <br /> Bubbling with a voice deeper than time, the cold water asked &quot;who am I?&quot;<br /> <br /> Gleeful with its own trickery, the Darkness pleasantly replied &quot;you are Death&quot;<br /> <br /> And Death whispered and flowed, drawing the rivers of Life toward it. And it poured bellow the earth, going down and down and gathering as a great ocean containing all of the fragments of Life, creating a world beneath the World to serve it as home- and the Darkness called it the underworld.<br /> <br /> Looking at all of its creation, the Darkness was pleased- yet the fear was yet to leave its black heart. For while it divided and ruled its children, one day perhaps they would unite against it- one day, the Truth and Shadow, Fate and Terror, Life and Death and the World may unit against its rule and overthrown it, throwing it from beyond the boundaries of the World for all eternity were it would starve for all eternity. It required something to unit them against each other, a single force which would make sure they would be bound forever in their struggle. And so, the Darkness gathered through the World, taking bits of each of its children- a shard of Truth, piece of Shadow, silver of Fate, pint of Terror, drop of Life, whisk of Death. It mixed them all in its own heart, and laid them in the World's loving embrace, making them the World's child as much as the World was its. And after nine times three times seven nights and days, the World called with pain of birth- fulfilling the curse its mother and father laid upon its centuries ago. From the earth they came, reaching to the sky and pulsing with the sea.<br /> <br /> Lonely and confused, they looked around themselves upon the strange gods and asked &quot;who am I?&quot;<br /> <br /> Kindly, its voice it dripping with honey, the Darkness replied &quot;you are Men&quot;<br /> <br /> With those words, the night has came- and then, there was darkness.</i><br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> so, the first part of a writing experiment in which I try to write a CofD mythology-cosmology thingy. Hope you'll like it!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T14:05:57-08:00","id":1042021,"title":"","content":"So. Calling back to the idea that Exalted is the pre-history of the World of Darkness, huh? The Ebon Dragon won, and then he created another world to define himself against <br /> <br /> At least, that's my theory. The references to a world before this brought it to mind","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T14:29:04-08:00","id":1042032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1041983-and-then-there-was-darkness-mythology-thread-just-for-fun?p=1042021#post1042021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So. Calling back to the idea that Exalted is the pre-history of the World of Darkness, huh? The Ebon Dragon won, and then he created another world to define himself against<br /> <br /> At least, that's my theory. The references to a world before this brought it to mind</div> </div> </div> </div>actually, it is a reference to the Classic World of Darkness. Exalted is the world before the world before :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T14:31:58-08:00","id":1042035,"title":"","content":"I was talking about the Classic world of Darkness","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T14:43:49-08:00","id":1042043,"title":"","content":"Also, just wanted to note that the main reason I've used the &quot;ruins from before&quot; is out of one common interpretation for the book of Genesis. In Hebrew, the first word in Genesis begins with the second letter of the Hebrew alphabet. Many claim it (and the references for the water, abyss, darkness and chaos) to mean that there was a world before the world created by God, and that Genesis simply tells the story of the current world we live in. This is why I've decided to start the text with &quot;And then&quot;, in honor for that interpretation. It is simply that the WoD's apocalyptic timeline makes it work as a possible &quot;world before&quot; for the setting, and one of the things I really want to do one day is having a Wod/CofD full crossover game. I have, however, never thought about the Ebon Dragon as the true identity of the &quot;Darkness&quot;- in my cosmology, it is simply the power of corruption which makes the setting of the CofD into what it is. Such connection is possible, of course, but not mandatory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}